---
title: Build Your Own Adapter
id: build-your-own-adapter
description: "Store chat history in the database you already run: implement one store, hand it to withPersistence, and prove it with the conformance suite."
keywords:
  - persistence adapter
  - custom store
  - conformance suite
  - drizzle prisma d1 adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your data lives in your own database (Postgres behind Prisma, a SQLite file, D1,\nMongo) and you do not want another service just for chat history. You do not need\none. An adapter is a plain object of store functions. The core never looks at your\ntables, so the schema stays yours."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"third-party-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Third-party adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you would rather use a ready-made backend, these adapters are published and maintained\noutside TanStack AI. Each one returns an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AIPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":", so the rest\nof this page applies unchanged."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Backend"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stores"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../community-adapters/upstash","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash Redis, plus Upstash Blob for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All seven"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintain an adapter? Add a row with a pull request. Run it against the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"conformance suite"}]},{"type":"text","value":" first, and list the stores it\npasses."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-smallest-adapter-that-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The smallest adapter that works"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One store, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", is enough for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":". This is the whole thing:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  defineAIPersistence,\n  defineMessageStore,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const persistence = defineAIPersistence({\n  stores: {\n    messages: defineMessageStore({\n      // Return [] for a thread that was never saved, never null.\n      loadThread: (threadId) => db.threads.messages(threadId),\n      // The full transcript, not a delta. Overwrite what you had.\n      saveThread: (threadId, messages) => db.threads.save(threadId, messages),\n    }),\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hand it to the middleware and you are done:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Already have tables? Nothing above assumes new ones. Name your columns whatever you\nlike, use your native types ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jsonb"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamptz"},{"type":"text","value":"), and convert inside the store\nfunctions. Extra columns such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user_id"},{"type":"text","value":" or audit timestamps are fine as long as\nthey are nullable or defaulted, because these stores never touch a column they do not\nknow about. There is one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"define*Store"},{"type":"text","value":" helper per store, and each type-checks your\nobject inline so you never annotate it by hand."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"which-stores-do-you-need","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which stores do you need?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each store switches on one capability. Find your column and implement the rows marked\nwith a tick:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"center","center","center","center","center","center","center"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save the transcript"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejoin a run after reload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable approvals"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App key/value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persist generation runs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep generated files"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rebuild sandbox files"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generationRuns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅"}]}]]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Columns stack."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Chat plus sandbox files means "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":" +\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":". Durable approvals plus generated files means the union of both\ncolumns."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two pairs cannot be split."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":"\nneeds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation runs need none of the chat stores."}]},{"type":"text","value":" See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox files need a checkpoint store too."}]},{"type":"text","value":" That store lives on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":", not in this table. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The common production shape is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":". When you\nkeep generated files or rebuild sandbox files, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also own only part of it. Put "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" in your database and fill\nthe rest from somewhere else with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"composePersistence"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { composePersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { messages, runs } from './my-postgres-stores'\n\nexport const persistence = composePersistence(memoryPersistence(), {\n  overrides: { messages, runs },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That gives you no transaction across the two systems, so a write touching both is two\nwrites. The store invariants (idempotent creates, insert-if-absent) are what make\nretrying them safe."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"let-your-agent-write-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let your agent write it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" ships "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that\nturn this into a recipe against your stack: your ORM config, your schema file, your\ndatabase handle."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then ask for \"add chat persistence to this app\". There are recipes for Drizzle,\nPrisma, Cloudflare D1, and anything else (raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pg"},{"type":"text","value":", Kysely, SQLite, Mongo, Supabase).\nThe skills are plain Markdown under\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules/@tanstack/ai-persistence/skills/"},{"type":"text","value":" if you would rather read them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prove it with the conformance suite"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not eyeball it. The same suite every packaged backend runs is shipped for yours. It\nexercises every method of every store you provide, including the ordering and\nidempotency rules that are easy to get subtly wrong."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('my sqlite adapter', () =>\n  sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Declare what you left out. A store you do not provide goes in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skip"},{"type":"text","value":", and an optional\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" method goes in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipMethods"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { chatOnlyPersistence } from './chat-only'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('chat-only adapter', () => chatOnlyPersistence(), {\n  skip: ['activities', 'generationRuns', 'artifacts', 'blobs'],\n  skipMethods: ['runs.listByThread'],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional run methods are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":". Add an omitted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":" to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipMethods"},{"type":"text","value":". An omitted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":" needs no entry: the subagent checks\nskip on their own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"turn-on-the-newer-checks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turn on the newer checks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some checks were added after the suite shipped. They are off by default, so an\nadapter that passed before still passes. Turn them on to prove that your adapter\nsupports run timings on reload ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeRuns: true"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance(\n  'my sqlite adapter',\n  () => sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n  { checks: ['messages.metadata', 'runs.listByThread.state'] },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages.metadata"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadThread"},{"type":"text","value":" returns each message's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" as it was saved."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs.listByThread.state"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":" returns each run's current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishedAt"},{"type":"text","value":" after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A check you do not turn on shows as skipped, with the option to add."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anything absent and undeclared fails with a message naming exactly what to add, so a\nhalf-wired adapter cannot report a pass. When this is green, your adapter is a drop-in\nfor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":", and with the generation stores for\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withGenerationPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./build-your-own-chat-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a chat adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the full SQLite walkthrough\nfor all four chat stores, method by method."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./build-your-own-generation-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a generation adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": generation runs,\nartifacts and blobs."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./build-a-sandbox-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a sandbox adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the sandbox instance store, and\nwhat a durable sandboxed run adds to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":". Only if you run sandboxes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":": reuse this\nadapter for portable snapshots. You need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./store-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every signature and invariant, and how the\nrecords relate."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controls"}]},{"type":"text","value":": compose stores from different systems."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./migrations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrations"}]},{"type":"text","value":": who owns the schema."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"third-party-adapters","text":"Third-party adapters","level":2},{"id":"the-smallest-adapter-that-works","text":"The smallest adapter that works","level":2},{"id":"which-stores-do-you-need","text":"Which stores do you need?","level":2},{"id":"let-your-agent-write-it","text":"Let your agent write it","level":2},{"id":"prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite","text":"Prove it with the conformance suite","level":2},{"id":"turn-on-the-newer-checks","text":"Turn on the newer checks","level":3},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour data lives in your own database (Postgres behind Prisma, a SQLite file, D1,\nMongo) and you do not want another service just for chat history. You do not need\none. An adapter is a plain object of store functions. The core never looks at your\ntables, so the schema stays yours.\n\n## Third-party adapters\n\nIf you would rather use a ready-made backend, these adapters are published and maintained\noutside TanStack AI. Each one returns an `AIPersistence` for `withPersistence`, so the rest\nof this page applies unchanged.\n\n| Adapter | Package | Backend | Stores |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [Upstash](../community-adapters/upstash) | `@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence` | Upstash Redis, plus Upstash Blob for `blobs` | All seven |\n\nMaintain an adapter? Add a row with a pull request. Run it against the\n[conformance suite](#prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite) first, and list the stores it\npasses.\n\n## The smallest adapter that works\n\nOne store, `messages`, is enough for `withPersistence`. This is the whole thing:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  defineAIPersistence,\n  defineMessageStore,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const persistence = defineAIPersistence({\n  stores: {\n    messages: defineMessageStore({\n      // Return [] for a thread that was never saved, never null.\n      loadThread: (threadId) => db.threads.messages(threadId),\n      // The full transcript, not a delta. Overwrite what you had.\n      saveThread: (threadId, messages) => db.threads.save(threadId, messages),\n    }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nHand it to the middleware and you are done:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})\n```\n\nAlready have tables? Nothing above assumes new ones. Name your columns whatever you\nlike, use your native types (`jsonb`, `timestamptz`), and convert inside the store\nfunctions. Extra columns such as `user_id` or audit timestamps are fine as long as\nthey are nullable or defaulted, because these stores never touch a column they do not\nknow about. There is one `define*Store` helper per store, and each type-checks your\nobject inline so you never annotate it by hand.\n\n## Which stores do you need?\n\nEach store switches on one capability. Find your column and implement the rows marked\nwith a tick:\n\n| Store | Save the transcript | Rejoin a run after reload | Durable approvals | App key/value | Persist generation runs | Keep generated files | Rebuild sandbox files |\n| --- | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\n| `messages` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n| `runs` | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `interrupts` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `metadata` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `generationRuns` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |\n| `artifacts` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| `blobs` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n\n- **Columns stack.** Chat plus sandbox files means `messages` + `artifacts` +\n  `blobs`. Durable approvals plus generated files means the union of both\n  columns.\n- **Two pairs cannot be split.** `interrupts` needs `runs`, and `artifacts`\n  needs `blobs`.\n- **Generation runs need none of the chat stores.** See\n  [Generation persistence](./generation-persistence).\n- **Sandbox files need a checkpoint store too.** That store lives on\n  `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`, not in this table. See\n  [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure).\n\nThe common production shape is `messages` + `runs` + `interrupts`. When you\nkeep generated files or rebuild sandbox files, add `artifacts` and `blobs`.\n\nYou can also own only part of it. Put `messages` and `runs` in your database and fill\nthe rest from somewhere else with `composePersistence`:\n\n```ts\nimport { composePersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { messages, runs } from './my-postgres-stores'\n\nexport const persistence = composePersistence(memoryPersistence(), {\n  overrides: { messages, runs },\n})\n```\n\nThat gives you no transaction across the two systems, so a write touching both is two\nwrites. The store invariants (idempotent creates, insert-if-absent) are what make\nretrying them safe.\n\n## Let your agent write it\n\n`@tanstack/ai-persistence` ships [Agent Skills](../getting-started/agent-skills) that\nturn this into a recipe against your stack: your ORM config, your schema file, your\ndatabase handle.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvue: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-persistence\npreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nangular: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-persistence\noctane: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nvue: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nsolid: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nsvelte: @tanstack/intent@latest install\npreact: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nangular: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nvanilla: @tanstack/intent@latest install\noctane: @tanstack/intent@latest install\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThen ask for \"add chat persistence to this app\". There are recipes for Drizzle,\nPrisma, Cloudflare D1, and anything else (raw `pg`, Kysely, SQLite, Mongo, Supabase).\nThe skills are plain Markdown under\n`node_modules/@tanstack/ai-persistence/skills/` if you would rather read them.\n\n## Prove it with the conformance suite\n\nDo not eyeball it. The same suite every packaged backend runs is shipped for yours. It\nexercises every method of every store you provide, including the ordering and\nidempotency rules that are easy to get subtly wrong.\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('my sqlite adapter', () =>\n  sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n)\n```\n\nDeclare what you left out. A store you do not provide goes in `skip`, and an optional\n`runs` method goes in `skipMethods`:\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { chatOnlyPersistence } from './chat-only'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('chat-only adapter', () => chatOnlyPersistence(), {\n  skip: ['activities', 'generationRuns', 'artifacts', 'blobs'],\n  skipMethods: ['runs.listByThread'],\n})\n```\n\nThe optional run methods are `listByThread`, `listByParentRun`, and\n`listReclaimable`. Add an omitted `listByThread` or `listReclaimable` to\n`skipMethods`. An omitted `listByParentRun` needs no entry: the subagent checks\nskip on their own.\n\n### Turn on the newer checks\n\nSome checks were added after the suite shipped. They are off by default, so an\nadapter that passed before still passes. Turn them on to prove that your adapter\nsupports run timings on reload (`reconstructChat` with `includeRuns: true`):\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance(\n  'my sqlite adapter',\n  () => sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n  { checks: ['messages.metadata', 'runs.listByThread.state'] },\n)\n```\n\n- `messages.metadata`: `loadThread` returns each message's `metadata` as it was saved.\n- `runs.listByThread.state`: `listByThread` returns each run's current `status` and `finishedAt` after `update`.\n\nA check you do not turn on shows as skipped, with the option to add.\n\nAnything absent and undeclared fails with a message naming exactly what to add, so a\nhalf-wired adapter cannot report a pass. When this is green, your adapter is a drop-in\nfor `withPersistence`, and with the generation stores for\n`withGenerationPersistence` too.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Build a chat adapter](./build-your-own-chat-adapter): the full SQLite walkthrough\n  for all four chat stores, method by method.\n- [Build a generation adapter](./build-your-own-generation-adapter): generation runs,\n  artifacts and blobs.\n- [Build a sandbox adapter](./build-a-sandbox-adapter): the sandbox instance store, and\n  what a durable sandboxed run adds to `runs`. Only if you run sandboxes.\n- [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure): reuse this\n  adapter for portable snapshots. You need `messages`, `artifacts`, and `blobs`.\n- [Store reference](./store-reference): every signature and invariant, and how the\n  records relate.\n- [Controls](./controls): compose stores from different systems.\n- [Migrations](./migrations): who owns the schema.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Build Your Own Adapter\nid: build-your-own-adapter\ndescription: \"Store chat history in the database you already run: implement one store, hand it to withPersistence, and prove it with the conformance suite.\"\nkeywords:\n  - persistence adapter\n  - custom store\n  - conformance suite\n  - drizzle prisma d1 adapter\n---\n\nYour data lives in your own database (Postgres behind Prisma, a SQLite file, D1,\nMongo) and you do not want another service just for chat history. You do not need\none. An adapter is a plain object of store functions. The core never looks at your\ntables, so the schema stays yours.\n\n## Third-party adapters\n\nIf you would rather use a ready-made backend, these adapters are published and maintained\noutside TanStack AI. Each one returns an `AIPersistence` for `withPersistence`, so the rest\nof this page applies unchanged.\n\n| Adapter | Package | Backend | Stores |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [Upstash](../community-adapters/upstash) | `@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence` | Upstash Redis, plus Upstash Blob for `blobs` | All seven |\n\nMaintain an adapter? Add a row with a pull request. Run it against the\n[conformance suite](#prove-it-with-the-conformance-suite) first, and list the stores it\npasses.\n\n## The smallest adapter that works\n\nOne store, `messages`, is enough for `withPersistence`. This is the whole thing:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  defineAIPersistence,\n  defineMessageStore,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const persistence = defineAIPersistence({\n  stores: {\n    messages: defineMessageStore({\n      // Return [] for a thread that was never saved, never null.\n      loadThread: (threadId) => db.threads.messages(threadId),\n      // The full transcript, not a delta. Overwrite what you had.\n      saveThread: (threadId, messages) => db.threads.save(threadId, messages),\n    }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nHand it to the middleware and you are done:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})\n```\n\nAlready have tables? Nothing above assumes new ones. Name your columns whatever you\nlike, use your native types (`jsonb`, `timestamptz`), and convert inside the store\nfunctions. Extra columns such as `user_id` or audit timestamps are fine as long as\nthey are nullable or defaulted, because these stores never touch a column they do not\nknow about. There is one `define*Store` helper per store, and each type-checks your\nobject inline so you never annotate it by hand.\n\n## Which stores do you need?\n\nEach store switches on one capability. Find your column and implement the rows marked\nwith a tick:\n\n| Store | Save the transcript | Rejoin a run after reload | Durable approvals | App key/value | Persist generation runs | Keep generated files | Rebuild sandbox files |\n| --- | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\n| `messages` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n| `runs` | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `interrupts` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `metadata` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |\n| `generationRuns` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |\n| `artifacts` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| `blobs` | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n\n- **Columns stack.** Chat plus sandbox files means `messages` + `artifacts` +\n  `blobs`. Durable approvals plus generated files means the union of both\n  columns.\n- **Two pairs cannot be split.** `interrupts` needs `runs`, and `artifacts`\n  needs `blobs`.\n- **Generation runs need none of the chat stores.** See\n  [Generation persistence](./generation-persistence).\n- **Sandbox files need a checkpoint store too.** That store lives on\n  `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`, not in this table. See\n  [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure).\n\nThe common production shape is `messages` + `runs` + `interrupts`. When you\nkeep generated files or rebuild sandbox files, add `artifacts` and `blobs`.\n\nYou can also own only part of it. Put `messages` and `runs` in your database and fill\nthe rest from somewhere else with `composePersistence`:\n\n```ts\nimport { composePersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { messages, runs } from './my-postgres-stores'\n\nexport const persistence = composePersistence(memoryPersistence(), {\n  overrides: { messages, runs },\n})\n```\n\nThat gives you no transaction across the two systems, so a write touching both is two\nwrites. The store invariants (idempotent creates, insert-if-absent) are what make\nretrying them safe.\n\n## Let your agent write it\n\n`@tanstack/ai-persistence` ships [Agent Skills](../getting-started/agent-skills) that\nturn this into a recipe against your stack: your ORM config, your schema file, your\ndatabase handle.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvue: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-persistence\npreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nangular: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-persistence\noctane: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nvue: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nsolid: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nsvelte: @tanstack/intent@latest install\npreact: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nangular: @tanstack/intent@latest install\nvanilla: @tanstack/intent@latest install\noctane: @tanstack/intent@latest install\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThen ask for \"add chat persistence to this app\". There are recipes for Drizzle,\nPrisma, Cloudflare D1, and anything else (raw `pg`, Kysely, SQLite, Mongo, Supabase).\nThe skills are plain Markdown under\n`node_modules/@tanstack/ai-persistence/skills/` if you would rather read them.\n\n## Prove it with the conformance suite\n\nDo not eyeball it. The same suite every packaged backend runs is shipped for yours. It\nexercises every method of every store you provide, including the ordering and\nidempotency rules that are easy to get subtly wrong.\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('my sqlite adapter', () =>\n  sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n)\n```\n\nDeclare what you left out. A store you do not provide goes in `skip`, and an optional\n`runs` method goes in `skipMethods`:\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { chatOnlyPersistence } from './chat-only'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance('chat-only adapter', () => chatOnlyPersistence(), {\n  skip: ['activities', 'generationRuns', 'artifacts', 'blobs'],\n  skipMethods: ['runs.listByThread'],\n})\n```\n\nThe optional run methods are `listByThread`, `listByParentRun`, and\n`listReclaimable`. Add an omitted `listByThread` or `listReclaimable` to\n`skipMethods`. An omitted `listByParentRun` needs no entry: the subagent checks\nskip on their own.\n\n### Turn on the newer checks\n\nSome checks were added after the suite shipped. They are off by default, so an\nadapter that passed before still passes. Turn them on to prove that your adapter\nsupports run timings on reload (`reconstructChat` with `includeRuns: true`):\n\n```ts\nimport { runPersistenceConformance } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence/testkit'\nimport { sqlitePersistence } from './sqlite-persistence'\n\nrunPersistenceConformance(\n  'my sqlite adapter',\n  () => sqlitePersistence({ url: ':memory:', migrate: true }),\n  { checks: ['messages.metadata', 'runs.listByThread.state'] },\n)\n```\n\n- `messages.metadata`: `loadThread` returns each message's `metadata` as it was saved.\n- `runs.listByThread.state`: `listByThread` returns each run's current `status` and `finishedAt` after `update`.\n\nA check you do not turn on shows as skipped, with the option to add.\n\nAnything absent and undeclared fails with a message naming exactly what to add, so a\nhalf-wired adapter cannot report a pass. When this is green, your adapter is a drop-in\nfor `withPersistence`, and with the generation stores for\n`withGenerationPersistence` too.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Build a chat adapter](./build-your-own-chat-adapter): the full SQLite walkthrough\n  for all four chat stores, method by method.\n- [Build a generation adapter](./build-your-own-generation-adapter): generation runs,\n  artifacts and blobs.\n- [Build a sandbox adapter](./build-a-sandbox-adapter): the sandbox instance store, and\n  what a durable sandboxed run adds to `runs`. Only if you run sandboxes.\n- [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure): reuse this\n  adapter for portable snapshots. You need `messages`, `artifacts`, and `blobs`.\n- [Store reference](./store-reference): every signature and invariant, and how the\n  records relate.\n- [Controls](./controls): compose stores from different systems.\n- [Migrations](./migrations): who owns the schema.\n"}
